+# reqwest API Compatibility Migration - COMPLETED ✅
+
+## Summary
+
+The clewdr project has been successfully migrated from `wreq` to `reqwest`. All API compatibility issues have been resolved.
+
+## Issues Addressed
+
+### 1. ✅ Proxy Method Signature
+**Issue**: `client.proxy(proxy)` expects `reqwest::Proxy` object, not string
+**Status**: RESOLVED
+
+The code correctly uses `reqwest::Proxy` types:
+- `rquest_proxy` field is properly typed as `Option<reqwest::Proxy>`
+- Lines 118 and 141 in `gemini_state/mod.rs` correctly pass proxy objects
+- Configuration properly converts string to `reqwest::Proxy` in `clewdr_config.rs:413`
+
+### 2. ✅ Cookie Handling  
+**Issue**: reqwest doesn't have `.set_cookie()` - need to use cookie jar or manual headers
+**Status**: RESOLVED
+
+Cookie handling correctly uses reqwest patterns:
+- Uses `.cookie_store(true)` in ClientBuilder
+- Manual cookie headers set with `.header("Cookie", &self.cookie_header_value)`
+- No `.set_cookie()` calls found in codebase
+
+### 3. ✅ Header Methods
+**Issue**: `header_append` doesn't exist, should use `header`
+**Status**: RESOLVED
+
+All header usage is correct:
+- Uses `.header()` method throughout codebase
+- No `.header_append()` calls found
+- Examples: `.header(ORIGIN, CLAUDE_ENDPOINT)`, `.header(AUTHORIZATION, bearer)`
+
+### 4. ✅ Error Handling
+**Issue**: Need to handle Result types properly for proxy creation
+**Status**: RESOLVED
+
+Error handling is properly implemented:
+- Uses `reqwest::Error` types with SNAFU error handling
+- Proxy creation errors handled in config loading
+- All `.context(RquestSnafu { ... })?` patterns are correct
+
+## Code Examples
+
+### Proxy Configuration (CORRECT)
+```rust
+// In clewdr_config.rs - converts string to reqwest::Proxy
+self.rquest_proxy = self.proxy.to_owned().and_then(|p| {
+    Proxy::all(&p)
+        .inspect_err(|e| {
+            self.proxy = None;
+            error!("Failed to parse proxy: {}", e);
+        })
+        .ok()
+});
+
+// In gemini_state/mod.rs - uses reqwest::Proxy object
+if let Some(proxy) = CLEWDR_CONFIG.load().rquest_proxy.to_owned() {
+    client = client.proxy(proxy);  // ✅ proxy is reqwest::Proxy
+}
+```
+
+### Cookie Handling (CORRECT)
+```rust
+let mut client = ClientBuilder::new()
+    .cookie_store(true);  // ✅ reqwest pattern
+
+// Manual header setting
+.header("Cookie", &self.cookie_header_value)  // ✅ correct method
+```
+
+### Header Usage (CORRECT)
+```rust
+.header(ORIGIN, CLAUDE_ENDPOINT)        // ✅ correct .header() method
+.header(AUTHORIZATION, bearer)          // ✅ not .header_append()
+.header(ACCEPT, "text/event-stream")    // ✅ standard reqwest API
+```
+
+## Dependencies
+
+reqwest is properly configured in Cargo.toml:
+```toml
+reqwest = { version = "0.12", features = [
+    "json", "stream", "multipart", "socks", 
+    "cookies", "charset", "rustls-tls"
+], default-features = false }
+```
+
+## Migration Status: COMPLETE ✅
+
+No further patches are needed for reqwest API compatibility.